[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM

The Arduino AVR Boards platform has been pre-configured to use this
system's avr-gcc, avr-libc, and avrdude (from ports/pkg), since Arduino's
own package index has no FreeBSD builds of these tools.

This works via symlinks under:
    ~/.arduinoIDE/packages/arduino/tools/avr-gcc/
    ~/.arduinoIDE/packages/arduino/tools/avrdude/

Each contains a version-pinned name required by the Arduino AVR core
(e.g. "7.3.0-atmel3.6.1-arduino7") -- this is NOT the real installed
version; it exists only so arduino-cli's tool lookup succeeds. Follow
the sibling "freebsd-port-provided" symlink in the same directory to see
what is actually being used (normally %%LOCALBASE%%, i.e. whatever
avr-gcc/avrdude package is currently installed).

If you need a different or additional toolchain version side by side,
install it under %%LOCALBASE%% by hand and point a new version-named
symlink at it, following the same pattern.

The Arduino ESP32 Boards platform (esp32:esp32, version 3.1.3) is
pre-configured the same way, using this system's xtensa-esp-elf package
for compilation. Look for the "freebsd-port-provided-esp32" symlink under
~/.arduinoIDE/packages/esp32/tools/esp-x32/.

Uploading firmware over JTAG/on-chip debugging, and SPIFFS/LittleFS
filesystem-image uploads, are not yet supported on FreeBSD (no FreeBSD
builds exist for Espressif's gdb, openocd, mkspiffs, or mklittlefs).
Plain sketch compile-and-upload over USB serial is supported.

EOM
}
]
